@startuml 01_overview
!include _style.iuml
title Timer1 functions: call graph and register access

package "Callers" {
  [setup()] as SETUP
  [loop()] as LOOP
}

package "Public API" {
  [setPWMMode(m)] as MODE
  [setPWMFrequency(f)] as FREQ
  [setPWMDuty(duty, pin)] as DUTY
  [pwmOn(pin) / pwmOff(pin)] as ONOFF
  [changePWMFrequency(f)] as CHG
}

package "Internal" {
  [setTimer(mode, f)] as SET
  [updatePins()] as UPD
  [ISR(TIMER1_OVF_vect)] as ISR
}

package "Helpers (only compute values)" {
  [wgmBits()] as WGM
  [dutyToOCR()] as D2O
  [comBits()] as COM
  [getControlWord()] as GCW
}

SETUP --> MODE
SETUP --> FREQ
SETUP --> DUTY
SETUP --> ONOFF
LOOP --> FREQ : set_pwm_freq changed
LOOP --> DUTY : set_pwm_duty9 changed
LOOP --> ONOFF : every pass

MODE --> SET : only if a frequency\nis already set
FREQ --> SET : f clamped to\n[lo, hi] limit
SET --> WGM
SET --> D2O
SET --> UPD
DUTY --> D2O
CHG --> D2O
ONOFF --> GCW
ONOFF --> UPD
UPD --> COM
CHG ..> ISR : arms (TOIE1)

note right of CHG
  Not called anywhere yet.
  For the ramp; needs
  FAST_PWM_PH_CORRECT (mode 8).
end note

legend bottom
  **Who writes which Timer1 register** (W = write, - = untouched)
  |= Function |= TCCR1A |= TCCR1B |= ICR1 |= OCR1A/B |= TCNT1 |= TIMSK1 |= TIFR1 |= PORTB |
  | setTimer | W (all) | W | W | W | W (=0) | W (TOIE1 off) | - | - |
  | updatePins | W (COM bits) | - | - | - | - | - | - | W (PB1/PB2 LOW) |
  | setPWMDuty | - | - | - | W | - | - | - | - |
  | changePWMFrequency | - | - | - | W | - | W (TOIE1 on) | W (clear TOV1) | - |
  | ISR(TIMER1_OVF) | - | - | W | - | - | W (TOIE1 off) | - | - |
  Helpers (wgmBits, comBits, dutyToOCR, getControlWord, isPwmMode) only compute values.
endlegend
@enduml
